    "lead": "Brief events can fall between uniformly sampled frames. EAS samples more densely around events and less densely where little changes, and TA-RoPE anchors every sampled frame to physical time — so predictions line up with the reference at matched physical times.",
    "caption_note": "Ceiling-view comparison from paper Fig. 6 (candidate 02): ground truth, fixed-rate baseline, and EAS with TA-RoPE share one playback timeline spanning 15.66 seconds of physical time. Each panel shows the same physical timestamp.",
